<XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xEC71C" flags="0x0">
    <title>0xEC71C Pilot 1 angle separation from main [code + drive validated]</title>
    <description># Pilot 1 angle — drive-log validation

Input: 2026-09-07-173652.csv; 12,832 unique samples over 1,402.8 seconds. Calibration assumed: 20260907_r002.bin. This assumption must match the flashed calibration.

## Finding

The normal Pilot 1 angle-separation table is at file offset **0xEC71C** (record header **0xEC6F0**), 10 × 10, big-endian 16-bit. Angle conversion used: raw × 0.0234375 degrees. Row axis: RPM; column axis: cycle injection quantity, raw × 0.01 mg/cycle.

Prediction: **IWVE1 ≈ IWHE1 + interpolate(EC71C, RPM, IMEIA)**.

Across 8,553 active steady samples (Pilot 1 quantity &gt; 0.05 mg and absolute RPM rate &lt; 60 rpm/s), average absolute error is 0.0901 degrees; median absolute error 0.0263 degrees; 98.92% are within 1 degree. Across all 11,225 active samples, average absolute error is 0.1572 degrees. Steady here only filters RPM rate, not all load transients. Diagnostic channels can be asynchronous.

RPM axis: [500.0, 800.0, 1000.0, 1500.0, 2000.0, 2500.0, 3000.0, 3500.0, 4200.0, 4800.0]

Quantity axis (mg/cycle): [0.0, 5.0, 10.0, 15.0, 20.0, 30.0, 40.0, 50.0, 60.0, 70.0]

## Executable evidence

Addresses below are raw MPC offsets, not external-flash runtime addresses.

- 0x41954 calls 0x4236C with RPM and cycle quantity.
- 0x4236C selects module slot 0x5C4. Its pointer resolves to external-flash file offset 0xEC6F0. Normal selection uses offset 0; alternatives use +0x244, +0x488 or +0x6CC according to event/state conditions.
- Normal table data begins at EC71C. Alternative data starts EC960, ECBA4 and ECDE0. Those alternatives fit this log substantially worse.
- 0x4197C–0x41998 adds normal-state angle corrections from r13 displacements 8DB4 and 8DB0.
- A parallel component is calculated through 0x42424, module slot 0x5C8 (ED000 base). Its four inspected time-component maps contain zero values in r002.
- Blending, duration/separation checks and limits follow. At 0x41AEC–0x41AF8 the angle path explicitly adds r13 displacement 8DA8, which the main-angle routine writes at 0x40C94 following its selector/correction calculation.
- Final angle component is stored at r13 displacement 8DB2 at 0x41F04–0x41F08, on the same accepted event branch that commits the experimentally supported Pilot 1 quantity.

This establishes a code-linked base angle separation and a very strong logged match. It does not establish every correction/alternate-state condition, nor independently complete the diagnostic B1 packet-source trace. Treat the logged signal as the requested angle component; this report does not independently validate physical injector opening or a BTDC sign convention.

## Quantity confirmation and correction

EEBE8 remains strongly supported as the Pilot 1 quantity table: with IMEIA and RPM, active-sample average absolute error is 0.03575 mg; steady error is 0.02545 mg. Main quantity is a significantly worse table-axis input across this drive.

Correction to earlier timing speculation: record EEDE8 is looked up at 0x41640 and compared against the corrected quantity result; the smaller value is retained before further quantity processing. It is a quantity-cap path, not the angle table identified above.

No calibration bytes or editor definitions were changed by this analysis. A change to EC71C shifts the base separation from main injection; the final result remains subject to the traced corrections and limits. Noise improvement from the quantity change does not on its own establish a benefit from changing separation.
</description>
